## `spec` fields

These are the top-level fields of the SandboxProfile spec, the same as `spec:` in YAML. Nested objects are described in the
server's JSON Schema at `GET /v1/schemas` (also used by the UI builder for validation).

| Field | Type | | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | optional |  |
| `backend` | string | optional |  Default: `local`. |
| `image` | string | optional | Container image or template (backend specific). |
| `cpu` | number | optional |  |
| `memory_mb` | number | optional |  |
| `disk_mb` | number | optional |  |
| `env` | map | optional |  |
| `workdir` | string | optional |  Default: `/workspace`. |
| `ttl` | string | optional |  Default: `PT4H`. |
| `network` | object | optional |  |
| `scope` | one of `step`, `run` | optional | 'run' shares one sandbox (and workspace) across all steps of a run. Default: `run`. |
| `suspend_on_wait` | bool | optional | Suspend run-scoped sandboxes during long waits. Default: `true`. |
| `config` | map | optional | Backend-specific settings. |

